          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಜಮಖಾನ — jamakhāna — \"a rug; a woven floor carpet\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಹಬ್ಬಕ್ಕೆ ನೆಲದ ಮೇಲೆ ಜಮಖಾನ ಹಾಸಿದರು. habbakke nelada mēle jamakhāna hāsidaru. They spread a rug on the floor for the festival."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Thick and woven, spread for guests to sit on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಜಮಖಾನ (jamakhāna) is usually traced to a Persian word that reached Kannada through Hindustani; the exact source is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
